validate or overwrite it. This creates a potential funds-redirection condition 
because Paraswap may send destination tokens to an arbitrary beneficiary. 
However, the supplied code does not conclusively demonstrate an exploitable 
theft path. In _deposit, the spell calculates the received amount from its own 
token balance and subsequently deposits that balance into the vault, while 
_withdraw later requires the swapped assets for repayment and refund. If the 
beneficiary is an attacker, these downstream checks will commonly underflow or 
fail, causing the transaction to revert rather than silently completing with 
stolen funds. Determining exploitability requires the omitted BasicSpell and 
Bank authorization/context logic, including whether untrusted callers can invoke
these functions for a live position and whether existing balances can satisfy 
downstream accounting. Therefore, the missing integration context prevents a 
